{
  "title": "Remember and surface each player's recently played games on the cabinet page",
  "open_questions": [
    {
      "id": "what-counts-as-played",
      "question": "What event records a game as played — opening its page from the cabinet, a game reporting a started round, or a finished round?",
      "required": true
    },
    {
      "id": "who-records-the-play",
      "question": "Does the cabinet record the play when it hands off to a game, or must each game under games/ report back, and if so how?",
      "required": true
    },
    {
      "id": "heading-wording",
      "question": "What exact heading text should sit above the recently played row?",
      "required": true
    },
    {
      "id": "first-visit-empty-state",
      "question": "On a first visit with nothing remembered, should the section be absent entirely or shown with placeholder copy?",
      "required": true
    },
    {
      "id": "duplicate-in-full-grid",
      "question": "Should a game appearing in the recently played row also still appear in the full grid below, or be omitted from it?",
      "required": true
    },
    {
      "id": "persistence-mechanism",
      "question": "Which storage mechanism and key name should hold the remembered plays (e.g. localStorage under a named key), and is per-browser scope acceptable with no accounts?",
      "required": true
    },
    {
      "id": "corrupt-state-recovery",
      "question": "When stored state is unreadable or malformed, should it be silently ignored, cleared and rewritten, or reported anywhere?",
      "required": true
    },
    {
      "id": "retired-game-cleanup",
      "question": "When a remembered game no longer exists in the catalogue, should it be dropped permanently from storage or just hidden while it is absent?",
      "required": true
    },
    {
      "id": "test-runner-scope",
      "question": "Does the declared `npm test` gate already execute acceptance/recently-played.test.js, or only tests/*.test.js?",
      "required": true
    },
    {
      "id": "unbound-criteria",
      "question": "acceptance/recently-played.test.js is the only check in the repository today that can fail on this feature, so dedupe-moves-to-front, cap-at-three, persists-across-sessions, catalogue-still-complete, survives-corrupt-state and tolerates-retired-game carry no gate binding — should new per-criterion checks be added, and where?",
      "required": true
    }
  ],
  "criteria": [
    {
      "id": "recent-section-renders",
      "title": "The cabinet page shows a recently played section above the full game grid, most recent first",
      "guidance": "Load index.html with remembered plays present; a distinct section appears before the full grid, listing those games in most-recent-first order, each entry launching that game.",
      "required": true,
      "human": false
    },
    {
      "id": "dedupe-moves-to-front",
      "title": "Replaying a game moves it to the front instead of adding a second entry",
      "guidance": "Record plays A, B, then A again; the remembered list is [A, B] with A first and no duplicate entry for A.",
      "required": true,
      "human": false
    },
    {
      "id": "cap-at-three",
      "title": "At most three games are remembered and shown",
      "guidance": "Record four distinct plays; the remembered list and the rendered section each contain exactly three entries, the three most recent, and the oldest is dropped.",
      "required": true,
      "human": false
    },
    {
      "id": "persists-across-sessions",
      "title": "Remembered plays survive closing the tab",
      "guidance": "Write plays, discard all in-memory state, re-read from the persistence layer as a fresh page load would, and get the same ordered list back.",
      "required": true,
      "human": false
    },
    {
      "id": "catalogue-still-complete",
      "title": "The full set of games remains listed below, unchanged",
      "guidance": "With and without remembered plays, the full grid still renders every game in src/catalogue.js in its existing order, and each still launches.",
      "required": true,
      "human": false
    },
    {
      "id": "survives-corrupt-state",
      "title": "Unexpected stored state cannot stop the page opening or a game starting",
      "guidance": "Seed the persistence layer with missing, empty, non-JSON, wrong-type and wrong-shape values in turn; in every case the page renders, no error escapes to the caller, and every game in the catalogue is still launchable.",
      "required": true,
      "human": false
    },
    {
      "id": "tolerates-retired-game",
      "title": "A remembered game that has left the catalogue does not break the page",
      "guidance": "Seed a remembered id that is absent from src/catalogue.js; the page renders, that entry is not shown as a broken tile, remaining remembered games still show, and every catalogued game still launches.",
      "required": true,
      "human": false
    },
    {
      "id": "heading-reads-as-yours",
      "title": "The section heading reads as the player's own history, not a recommendation",
      "guidance": "A person reads the heading and surrounding copy and judges that it obviously means \"games you played\" rather than \"games we suggest\".",
      "required": true,
      "human": true
    },
    {
      "id": "existing-gates-still-green",
      "title": "The repository's own lint and test gates still pass",
      "guidance": "npm run lint and npm test both pass after the change.",
      "required": true,
      "human": false
    }
  ],
  "gates": [
    {
      "id": "lint",
      "run": "npm run lint"
    },
    {
      "id": "test",
      "run": "npm test"
    }
  ],
  "gate_bindings": [
    {
      "id": "acceptance-recently-played",
      "run": "node --test acceptance/recently-played.test.js",
      "proves": "recent-section-renders"
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "recent-plays-store",
      "brief": "briefs/recent-plays-store.md",
      "dir": ".",
      "objective": "Build the module that remembers plays: a record function that pushes a game id to the front of the list, removes any existing entry for that id rather than duplicating it, and truncates to three entries, plus a read function that returns the remembered ids most-recent-first. It must persist across page loads using the mechanism settled in the persistence-mechanism question, and its read path must treat missing, empty, non-JSON, wrong-type and wrong-shape stored values as \"nothing remembered\" without throwing. Done when the store can be written and re-read as a fresh session would, and no seeded garbage value can make either function raise.",
      "objective_note": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "cabinet-recent-section",
      "brief": "briefs/cabinet-recent-section.md",
      "dir": ".",
      "objective": "Render the remembered games as a section in src/cabinet.js and index.html, placed above the existing full grid, listing the remembered games most-recent-first with the heading agreed in the heading-wording question, and each entry launching its game. Remembered ids that no longer resolve to an entry in src/catalogue.js are skipped rather than rendered. The full grid below keeps listing every catalogued game exactly as it does today. Done when acceptance/recently-played.test.js passes and the page still renders and launches every game when the remembered list is empty, partly stale, or entirely stale.",
      "objective_note": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "record-plays-on-launch",
      "brief": "briefs/record-plays-on-launch.md",
      "dir": ".",
      "objective": "Wire the recording side: whenever a play happens as defined by the what-counts-as-played and who-records-the-play answers, the store is updated with that game's id. The recording call must never be able to prevent the game from starting — a failure in storage is swallowed and the launch proceeds. Done when launching each game from the cabinet leaves that game at the front of the remembered list on the next page load, and a deliberately broken storage layer still lets every game start.",
      "objective_note": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "resilience-coverage",
      "brief": "briefs/resilience-coverage.md",
      "dir": ".",
      "objective": "Extend tests/cabinet.test.js and tests/catalogue.test.js with the cases that currently have no check: dedupe-moves-to-front, the three-entry cap, read-back after a simulated fresh session, the full grid still containing every catalogued game, each malformed stored value leaving the page renderable and every game launchable, and a remembered id absent from the catalogue being skipped without breaking the rest. Done when these cases exist as named tests, fail against the pre-feature behaviour, and pass under npm test with the feature in place.",
      "objective_note": ""
    }
  ]
}
